rom Cinema 4D (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from houdini (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-houdini\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-houdini-beta-2\">Publish from Houdini (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from solidworks (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-solidworks\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-solidworks-beta-2\">Publish from SolidWorks (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from spline, and figma (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-spline\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-spline-and-figma-beta-2\">Publish from Spline, and Figma (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"camera paths and default walkthroughs\" href=\"/docs/guides/camera-paths\" id=\"lnk-camera-paths-and-default-walkthroughs-2\">Camera paths and default walkthroughs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"hotspots and doors\" href=\"/docs/guides/hotspots-and-doors\" id=\"lnk-hotspots-and-doors-2\">Hotspots and doors</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse capture: film a room (beta)\" href=\"/docs/guides/film-a-room\" id=\"lnk-verse-capture-film-a-room-beta-2\">Verse Capture: film a room (beta)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse play: host a web game\" href=\"/docs/guides/host-a-web-game\" id=\"lnk-verse-play-host-a-web-game-2\">Verse Play: host a web game</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"spatial bench\" href=\"/docs/guides/spatial-bench\" id=\"lnk-spatial-bench-2\">Spatial Bench</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"light and dark theme\" href=\"/docs/guides/light-and-dark-theme\" id=\"lnk-light-and-dark-theme-2\">Light and dark theme</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"share privately with tokens\" href=\"/docs/guides/share-privately\" id=\"lnk-share-privately-with-tokens-2\">Share privately with tokens</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"show your clients who looked\" href=\"/docs/guides/analytics\" id=\"lnk-show-your-clients-who-looked-2\">Show your clients who looked</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed anywhere: wordpress, shopify, webflow\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-anywhere\" id=\"lnk-embed-anywhere-wordpress-shopify-webflow-2\">Embed anywhere: WordPress, Shopify, Webflow</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse for commerce: 3d on product pages (woocommerce, magento, bigcommerce, salesforce)\" href=\"/docs/guides/commerce\" id=\"lnk-verse-for-commerce-3d-on-product-pages-w-2\">Verse for Commerce: 3D on product pages (WooCommerce, Magento, BigCommerce, Salesforce)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse links and embeds: embed the viewer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-the-viewer\" id=\"lnk-verse-links-and-embeds-embed-the-viewer-2\">Verse links and embeds: embed the viewer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"export a flythrough video\" href=\"/docs/guides/export-video\" aria-current=\"page\" id=\"lnk-export-a-flythrough-video-2\">Export a flythrough video</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"collect client review comments\" href=\"/docs/guides/collect-review-comments\" id=\"lnk-collect-client-review-comments-2\">Collect client review comments</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"author a guided tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/author-a-guided-tour\" id=\"lnk-author-a-guided-tour-2\">Author a guided tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"video on surfaces, sound in the room\" href=\"/docs/guides/video-and-audio\" id=\"lnk-video-on-surfaces-sound-in-the-room-2\">Video on surfaces, sound in the room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"publish from ifc or usd\" href=\"/docs/guides/publish-from-ifc\" id=\"lnk-publish-from-ifc-or-usd-2\">Publish from IFC or USD</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"upload fbx and obj\" href=\"/docs/guides/upload-fbx-obj\" id=\"lnk-upload-fbx-and-obj-2\">Upload FBX and OBJ</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"build a configurator\" href=\"/docs/guides/build-a-configurator\" id=\"lnk-build-a-configurator-2\">Build a configurator</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"present a scene to a room\" href=\"/docs/guides/present-a-scene\" id=\"lnk-present-a-scene-to-a-room-2\">Present a scene to a room</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse-prepare: the local compression step\" href=\"/docs/guides/verse-prepare\" id=\"lnk-verse-prepare-the-local-compression-step-2\">verse-prepare: the local compression step</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"tune quality knobs\" href=\"/docs/guides/tune-quality\" id=\"lnk-tune-quality-knobs-2\">Tune quality knobs</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"run your own server\" href=\"/docs/guides/run-your-own-server\" id=\"lnk-run-your-own-server-2\">Run your own server</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"monitor production\" href=\"/docs/guides/monitor-production\" id=\"lnk-monitor-production-2\">Monitor production</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"ask verse, the site assistant\" href=\"/docs/guides/ask-verse\" id=\"lnk-ask-verse-the-site-assistant-2\">Ask Verse, the site assistant</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: floor plan to 3d home\" href=\"/docs/guides/floor-plan-to-3d\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-floor-plan-to-3d-home-2\">Verse Home: floor plan to 3D home</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour\" href=\"/docs/guides/instant-home\" id=\"lnk-verse-home-plan-to-a-home-buyers-walk-re-2\">Verse Home: plan to a home buyers walk, restyle and tour</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page\" href=\"/docs/guides/web-component\" id=\"lnk-one-tag-any-page-2\">&lt;verse-viewer&gt;: one tag, any page</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"designer tools: framer, webflow, figma\" href=\"/docs/guides/designer-tools\" id=\"lnk-designer-tools-framer-webflow-figma-2\">Designer tools: Framer, Webflow, Figma</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"react and vue wrappers\" href=\"/docs/guides/react-and-vue\" id=\"lnk-react-and-vue-wrappers-2\">React and Vue wrappers</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"rest client round trip\" href=\"/docs/guides/rest-client\" id=\"lnk-rest-client-round-trip-2\">REST client round trip</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with woocommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-woocommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-woocommerce-2\">Sell with WooCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with bigcommerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-bigcommerce\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-bigcommerce-2\">Sell with BigCommerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"sell with magento / adobe commerce\" href=\"/docs/guides/sell-with-magento\" id=\"lnk-sell-with-magento-adobe-commerce-2\">Sell with Magento / Adobe Commerce</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in wix\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-wix\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-wix-2\">Embed in Wix</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in squarespace\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-squarespace\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-squarespace-2\">Embed in Squarespace</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in framer\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-framer\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-framer-2\">Embed in Framer</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed in ghost and hubspot\" href=\"/docs/guides/embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot\" id=\"lnk-embed-in-ghost-and-hubspot-2\">Embed in Ghost and HubSpot</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with zapier\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-zapier\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-zapier-2\">Automate with Zapier</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with make\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-make\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-make-2\">Automate with Make</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"automate with n8n\" href=\"/docs/guides/automate-with-n8n\" id=\"lnk-automate-with-n8n-2\">Automate with n8n</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-10\"><h2>Blog & updates</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"all posts\" href=\"/docs/blog/index\" id=\"lnk-all-posts-2\">All posts</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"how verse streams a building\" href=\"/docs/blog/how-verse-streams-a-building\" id=\"lnk-how-verse-streams-a-building-2\">How Verse streams a building</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.7: what's new for you\" href=\"/docs/blog/verse-engine-2-7-whats-new\" id=\"lnk-2-7-what-s-new-for-you-2\">2.7: what's new for you</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"2.0 release notes for humans\" href=\"/docs/blog/2-0-release-notes-for-humans\" id=\"lnk-2-0-release-notes-for-humans-2\">2.0 release notes for humans</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-11\"><h2>Integrations</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"integrations: every platform at a glance\" href=\"/docs/integrations\" id=\"lnk-integrations-every-platform-at-a-glance-2\">Integrations: every platform at a glance</a></section><section id=\"sec-item-12\"><h2>API & SDK</h2><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api, sdk and mcp: embed, sdk, webhooks\" href=\"/docs/developers\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-sdk-and-mcp-embed-sdk-webhooks-2\">Verse API, SDK and MCP: embed, SDK, webhooks</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse api reference\" href=\"/docs/api\" id=\"lnk-verse-api-reference-2\">Verse API reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api quickstart\" href=\"/docs/api-quickstart\" id=\"lnk-api-quickstart-2\">API quickstart</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"api changelog\" href=\"/docs/api-changelog\" id=\"lnk-api-changelog-2\">API changelog</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"embed sdk reference\" href=\"/docs/embed-sdk\" id=\"lnk-embed-sdk-reference-2\">Embed SDK reference</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse sdk: js / ts (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)\" href=\"/docs/sdk\" id=\"lnk-verse-sdk-js-ts-ctruhtech-verse-sdk-2\">Verse SDK: JS / TS (@ctruhtech/verse-sdk)</a><a data-doc-item data-doc-title=\"verse mcp server for ai agents\" href=\"/docs/mcp\" id=\"lnk-verse-mcp-server-for-ai-agents-2\">Verse MCP server for AI agents</a></section><p class=\"docs-no-results\" hidden>No matching guides.</p></div></nav></aside><div class=\"doc-body\"><article class=\"doc-article\" id=\"art-doc-article\"><h1 id=\"export-a-flythrough-video\">Export a flythrough video<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#export-a-flythrough-video\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section\">#</a></h1>\n<p>Every streamed scene can become a client-ready MP4 or WebM — recorded from\nthe live engine, in the viewer&#39;s own browser, with nothing uploaded and no\nserver render farm. Two ways to get one: a button in the playground, or\n<code>exportVideo()</code> in an embed.</p>\n<p><strong>You need:</strong> a scene that has a tour. Scenes compiled with auto-staging\nalready do (the server writes a ~30 s loop into <code>&lt;id&gt;.stage.json</code>: an orbit\nfor open-sky scenes, a walkthrough through the largest open rooms for\ninteriors). A recorded tour (<code>?tour=</code>) works too, and in embeds a scene\nwith no tour at all gets a synthesized orbit of its framing sphere.</p>\n<h2 id=\"from-the-playground\">From the playground<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#from-the-playground\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-2\">#</a></h2>\n<ol><li>Open the share link. Once the scene is up, a <strong>Tour</strong> chip appears —\nand beside it, <strong>Export video</strong>.</li><li>Click it and pick <strong>duration</strong> (defaults to the tour length),\n<strong>resolution</strong> (1080p / 720p / native) and go.</li><li>The file downloads as <code>&lt;scene&gt;-tour.mp4</code> (H.264, where the browser can\nmux MP4: Chrome/Edge 126+, Safari) or <code>.webm</code> (VP9 elsewhere). The chip\nis labelled with the container you will actually get.</li></ol>\n<p>During capture the engine pins render scale to 1 (no dynamic resolution),\nblocks on-demand parking, and runs the render target at the output\nresolution; everything restores afterwards, including on cancel.</p>\n<p>For scripting and QA the same thing is one call in the page console:</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"js\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-js\">await window.__verseExportVideo({ duration: 10, fps: 30, height: 1080, format: &quot;mp4&quot;, download: true });\n// resolves the Blob; download:false keeps it in memory</code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"from-an-embed\">From an embed<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#from-an-embed\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-3\">#</a></h2>\n<p>The capture runs <strong>inside the engine iframe</strong> (that is where the canvas\nlives) and the finished bytes transfer to your page as a <code>Blob</code>, so your\npage decides: download, upload to your own storage, or preview inline.</p>\n<div class=\"doc-code\" data-lang=\"html\"><div><span>Code</span><button type=\"button\" data-copy-local id=\"btn-copy-2\">Copy ⧉</button></div><pre><code class=\"lang-html\">&lt;div id=&quot;viewer&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;button id=&quot;make-video&quot;&gt;Export video&lt;/button&gt; &lt;button id=&quot;cancel&quot; hidden&gt;Cancel&lt;/button&gt;\n&lt;progress id=&quot;bar&quot; max=&quot;100&quot; value=&quot;0&quot; hidden&gt;&lt;/progress&gt;\n&lt;script src=&quot;https://HOST/embed.js&quot;&gt;&lt;/script&gt;\n&lt;script&gt;\n  const viewer = Verse.embed(document.getElementById(&quot;viewer&quot;), { scene: &quot;docs-demo-718035483f84&quot; });\n  const bar = document.getElementById(&quot;bar&quot;), cancel = document.getElementById(&quot;cancel&quot;);\n  viewer.on(&quot;export-progress&quot;, (p) =&gt; (bar.value = p.percent));\n\n  document.getElementById(&quot;make-video&quot;).onclick = async () =&gt; {\n    bar.hidden = cancel.hidden = false;\n    try {\n      const r = await viewer.exportVideo({ duration: 10, fps: 30, height: 1080 });\n      if (!r.cancelled) {\n        // r.blob is yours. Download it…\n        const a = Object.assign(document.createElement(&quot;a&quot;), { href: URL.createObjectURL(r.blob), download: r.name });\n        a.click();\n        // …or upload it: fetch(&quot;/my/upload&quot;, { method: &quot;POST&quot;, body: r.blob })\n      }\n    } catch (e) {\n      console.warn(&quot;export failed:&quot;, e.message);   // &quot;no scene loaded yet&quot;, &quot;an export is already running&quot;\n    } finally {\n      bar.hidden = cancel.hidden = true;\n    }\n  };\n  cancel.onclick = () =&gt; viewer.cancelExport();     // the pending promise resolves { cancelled: true }\n&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre></div>\n<h3 id=\"options\">Options<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#options\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-4\">#</a></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Default</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>duration</code></td><td>tour length</td><td>seconds, clamped 1–600</td></tr><tr><td><code>fps</code></td><td><code>30</code></td><td>clamped 5–60</td></tr><tr><td><code>height</code></td><td><code>1080</code></td><td>output height in px; <code>0</code> = the canvas&#39;s native height</td></tr><tr><td><code>format</code></td><td>auto (MP4 where supported)</td><td><code>&quot;mp4&quot;</code> or <code>&quot;webm&quot;</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>bitrate</code></td><td>~10 Mbps at 1080p, scaled by area</td><td>video bits per second</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p>Resolves <code>{ blob, mimeType, name, width, height, frames, cancelled }</code>. One\nexport runs at a time; <code>export-progress</code> events fire per captured frame and\nan <code>export-done</code> <code>{ id, size, cancelled, error? }</code> event summarises the run\nfor analytics (the bytes ride the promise, not the event).</p>\n<h3 id=\"without-the-sdk\">Without the SDK<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#without-the-sdk\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-5\">#</a></h3>\n<p>If you talk to the iframe yourself, three messages do the job:\n<code>verse:export-video</code> <code>{ id, duration?, fps?, height?, format?, bitrate? }</code>\ndown; <code>verse:event</code> <code>{ name: &quot;export-progress&quot;, detail: { id, percent,\nframe, total } }</code> up while capturing; finally <code>verse:export-video-done</code>\n<code>{ id, bytes (transferred ArrayBuffer), mime, name, width, height, frames,\ncancelled }</code> — or <code>{ id, error }</code> on refusal (busy, no scene, recording\nunsupported). <code>verse:export-video-cancel</code> <code>{ id }</code> cancels.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-a-better-video\">Getting a better video<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#getting-a-better-video\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\" id=\"lnk-link-to-this-section-6\">#</a></h2>\n<ul><li>Pick the camera path first. Record your own with the editor&#39;s ⏺\n<strong>Record tour</strong> (<code>&amp;edit=1</code>), publish it with <code>POST /v1/tour</code>, and open the\nscene through the resulting <code>?tour=</code> link before exporting.</li><li>1080p at 30 fps is the sweet spot for listings and review decks; <code>height:\n0</code> captures the panel&#39;s native resolution when you need 4K from a 4K\ndisplay.</li><li>The export records exactly what the viewer renders, so quality knobs\napply: see <a href=\"/docs/guides/tune-quality\" id=\"lnk-tune-quality-knobs-3\">Tune quality knobs</a> — <code>?scale=1</code> is pinned\nfor you, <code>?ssr=1</code> and <code>?hdr=0</code> are worth setting explicitly for a video\ndestined for SDR screens.</li></ul></article><div class=\"doc-source\">Published documentation from <a href=\"https://verse.ctruh.com/docs/#/guides/export-video\" id=\"lnk-verse-by-ctruh\">Verse by Ctruh</a></div></div><aside class=\"docs-toc\" id=\"asd-docs-toc\"><p>ON THIS PAGE</p><a href=\"#from-the-playground\" id=\"lnk-from-the-playground\">From the playground</a><a href=\"#from-an-embed\" id=\"lnk-from-an-embed\">From an embed</a><a href=\"#getting-a-better-video\" id=\"lnk-getting-a-better-video\">Getting a better video</a></aside></section>"}